  "notes": "A godan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}) meaning to begin or set about doing something. Takes the particle に to mark the task being started.\n\nGodan verb with る ending. Dictionary form: {取|と}り{掛|か}かる. Te-form: {取|と}り{掛|か}かって. Past: {取|と}り{掛|か}かった.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～に{取|と}り{掛|か}かる: to start working on ~\n- すぐに{取|と}り{掛|か}かる: to get right on it\n- {早速|さっそく}{取|と}り{掛|か}かる: to set about it at once\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {始|はじ}める: to begin — general purpose, more neutral\n- {着手|ちゃくしゅ}する: to commence, to embark on — more formal, used for projects or official tasks\n\n{取|と}り{掛|か}かる emphasizes the act of physically getting started on a task, implying rolling up one's sleeves and diving in.",
